WEBVTT

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.850
<b>Machida Station\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hSouth Exit</b>

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:13.890
Let me carry that.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:19.930
Uh, but...

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.000
<u>Episode 11</u>
<b>Peridot of Blessings</b>

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.800
<b>Inamura</b>

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.580
Right this way.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:04.470
Sorry for making you do this.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:06.330
What are you talking about?

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:10.150
If I didn't at least treat you to some tea, 
the gods would surely punish me.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.620
<b>L
e
s

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:23.620
Huh?

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.310
Isn't this...

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:26.100
<b>L
e
s

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:26.150
<b>L
e
s

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:26.400
<b>L
e
s

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:26.880
<b>L
e
s

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.630
Thank you for waiting.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:37.720
Do you like Hugo?

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:41.310
I'm reading that right now 
on a recommendation.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:44.680
I just got to the part where 
he steals the silverware.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:48.060
I feel really bad for the protagonist.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:53.120
No one who feels sorry for Jean Valjean 
before his encounter with the bishop

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:54.570
is a bad person.

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:56.070
Huh?

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.860
<i>No one who feels sorry for Jean Valjean 
before his encounter with the bishop</i>

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.660
<i>is a bad person.</i>

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:07.970
Is there something on my face?

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:09.240
Oh, no.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.200
Pudding...

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.310
Do young folks not like pudding?

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:19.220
No, I love it.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.100
Thanks for the treat.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:30.050
This isn't ordinary sugar, is it?

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:31.920
I'm impressed you can tell.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:37.400
It's honey... No, black sugar?

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:39.740
Well done.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:40.780
Huh?

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.590
Oh, I'm sorry. Old habits die hard.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:47.240
Despite how I seem now, 
I used to be a teacher.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.350
Really?

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:51.800
I was a tutor before I became a teacher.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:56.590
I'd always tell the children they'd done well 
when I rewarded them with pudding.

00:03:56.930 --> 00:03:57.740
What?

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:02.300
Um, could I ask you a strange question?

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.940
What is it?

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:07.080
That photo was taken in England, wasn't it?

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:07.810
Yes.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:11.730
That's Count Claremont's residence, right?

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:17.900
Does the name "Richard" 
ring a bell, by any chance?

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.700
Richard-san...

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:24.740
I work at Richard's shop.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:31.050
I was just thinking it'd be an incredible 
coincidence if you're Richard's governess.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:37.920
I'll make some more tea.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:48.200
Thank you so much for today. 
I appreciate the help.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.370
No, thank you for the tea and pudding.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:53.230
Excuse me...

00:04:55.210 --> 00:05:00.940
I hate to ask such a thing of a 
nice young man such as yourself,

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:04.950
but please keep the fact 
that we met between us.

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:05.990
What?

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.920
It tastes different today, doesn't it?

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:25.670
I demand an explanation.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.300
An explanation?

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.990
An explanation, huh?

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:35.560
Um... the other day, when I went
to visit my mom, Hiromi...

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:36.640
Seigi.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:41.270
I'm sorry, but I can't tell you.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:47.470
I see. So that's the only 
explanation you can give...

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:54.230
Come to think of it,

00:05:54.230 --> 00:06:00.540
I haven't told you why 
I still use the name "de Vulpian."

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:03.300
Does that have anything to do with this?

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:09.320
I'm searching for a Japanese woman 
who once took care of me.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:11.890
I took my mother's maiden name

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:16.090
so that she'd recognize me 
immediately if she ever saw it.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:21.680
For three years, between 
the ages of six to nine,

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:23.780
I learned Japanese from her.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:28.320
<b>22 Years Ago</b>

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:31.040
At the time, my parents were already divorced,

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:33.920
and I was living with my uncle.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:40.040
Full marks for both of you. Well done.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.100
Yes! We get pudding!

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:44.450
I'm going to show Mother!

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:55.650
Young Master Richard, 
you did a very good job, too.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:05.020
<b>3 Years Later</b>

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:14.660
What are we going to do about Ashcroft?

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:19.660
Did something happen with 
Young Master Richard's father?

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:24.500
He's going to reconcile with Catherine 
and move to the Amazon.

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:26.540
The Amazon?

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:30.230
It's probably just for appearances.

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:36.970
It's easier for an entomologist to get 
through immigration with a family.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:39.910
Then will Young Master Richard
be going to the Amazon, as well?

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:40.730
Indeed.

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:43.930
But if the family will all be together,

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.280
that's a great thing for him.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:50.260
Catherine is an actress through and through.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:52.310
She's no mother.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:13.990
Richard!

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:15.180
Maman...

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:17.050
Don't call me that.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.930
I'm sorry, Catherine.

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:23.390
Escort me, Richard.

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:46.970
Merry Christmas.

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:48.840
Merry Christmas!

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:54.190
It happened on Christmas night...

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:00.390
What is it, Catherine?

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:03.890
It's gone... My necklace is missing!

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:11.050
The piece in question was a 19th-century 
antique set with a large peridot.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:14.780
It was transformable jewelry 
that could be taken apart.

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:26.910
We searched everywhere 
and still couldn't find it.

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:30.990
Perhaps you've just forgotten 
that you left it somewhere else.

00:09:30.990 --> 00:09:33.760
It was there when I went to rest in my room,

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.150
and when I woke up, it was gone!

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:38.260
Someone must've taken it.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:41.450
Let me go through your belongings.

00:09:43.210 --> 00:09:45.270
Here we go again...

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.730
The queen is on a rampage.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.020
Catherine, that's enough.

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:52.980
There aren't any thieves here!

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:55.500
Are you sure about that?

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:56.320
What?

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:59.380
You think Chieko took it?

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:03.290
A poor student would need the money, after all.

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:09.290
Stop this, Catherine.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:14.000
My, my... Look at this.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:21.510
What's my necklace's clasp 
doing inside your bag?

00:10:27.150 --> 00:10:30.730
It's too hasty to assume she did 
it on the basis of that alone.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:35.070
Chieko, we're all on your side.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:37.400
If there's some explanation for this, tell us.

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:41.450
I...

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:56.490
In the end, we never found the necklace.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:11:00.340
For that and other reasons, 
my parents didn't reconcile...

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:04.220
and that was the last I ever saw of Chieko.

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:06.720
I see.

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:11.810
But I absolutely must see her again.

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:18.840
Seigi, Japan has a tradition 
of visiting people to thank them.

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:22.090
It's considered polite to bring a gift

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:25.850
to the home of someone 
who has been hospitable to you.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:27.740
It's a fantastic tradition.

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:30.420
Don't you agree?

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:34.590
I do.

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:45.160
I'm sorry.

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:47.470
I couldn't keep it to myself.

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:50.270
I had a feeling this would happen.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:54.450
But as I mentioned the other day,

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:57.320
a lot happened between me 
and Young Master Richard.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:02.450
Um, I came with a message from him today.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:03.910
A message?

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.040
Yes.

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:09.370
Regarding the particulars of what 
happened on Christmas nineteen years ago.

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:17.460
What did Young Master Richard tell you?

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:21.970
No, I should explain myself.

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:27.940
I don't know if I did the right thing.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:36.140
All I can say for certain is that 
I hurt Young Master Richard.

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:43.400
Today is... a very... auspicious day...

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:43.110
<b>22 Years Ago</b>

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:45.610
Now say your greetings in Japanese.

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:48.330
Nice to meet you, Chieko.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.500
It's good to see you.

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:54.810
Well done, both of you.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.710
Here. This is your reward.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:06.730
The children adore you.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.160
Keep up the good work.

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:11.930
I'll do my best not to disappoint.

00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:23.870
<i>Les Misérables</i>...

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:26.370
Thank you, Chieko!

00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:32.930
Why do these things keep 
happening to Jean Valjean?

00:13:32.930 --> 00:13:34.370
I feel bad for him.

00:13:35.180 --> 00:13:39.340
No one who feels sorry for Jean Valjean 
before his encounter with the bishop

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:40.840
is a bad person.

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:43.820
You're a good boy, Young Master Richard.

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:46.730
Where's Young Master Jeffrey?

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:49.100
He has a cold.

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:52.100
Auntie is caring for him at his bedside.

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:04.490
If you catch a cold, I'll take care of you.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.020
It's a promise.

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:19.270
Three years passed in the blink of an eye,

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:21.170
<b>3 Years Later</b>

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:22.630
and the day I was to return to 
Japan was fast approaching.

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:27.470
Chieko, if you were to 
take work with us formally,

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.950
we'd pay you appropriately.

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:33.140
What? But I'm going back to Japan...

00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:38.570
At home, isn't your only option to get 
married and become a housewife?

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:43.430
You should instead remain here, 
where you can study all you'd like.

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:45.650
I appreciate the offer, but...

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:49.030
There's no need to hold back, Chieko.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:53.710
In the first place, do you have any idea 
how sad Richard will be if you leave?

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:57.530
Richard loves you like a mother.

00:14:57.530 --> 00:15:00.730
You don't want to leave him either, do you?

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:01.670
I...

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:08.650
I trust that you won't betray me, Chieko.

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:24.280
Then, that fated Christmas day...

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:31.370
Lady Catherine summoned me to 
the garden at the edge of the lawn.

00:15:32.370 --> 00:15:34.030
I have a request.

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:37.480
For me?

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:44.040
Think of it not as helping me, 
but helping Richard.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.220
What?

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:49.150
You know Ashcroft is planning 
to reconcile with me, don't you?

00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:49.970
Yes.

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:52.800
I want to wipe the slate clean.

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:56.260
You're not going to get back together?

00:15:56.790 --> 00:16:02.300
No. I've realized this is best for Richard.

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:11.290
Honestly, at first, I wanted 
to take him back from you.

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:13.500
That made me want to reconcile.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:17.800
But that boy is part of the count's family.

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:20.820
He should receive an appropriate education.

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:25.340
It's best for Richard to stay here.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:29.420
Are you okay with staying like this?

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:32.750
Me?

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:38.720
<i>I trust that you won't betray me, Chieko.</i>

00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:47.110
Please let me help you, Lady Catherine.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:49.070
Are you sure?

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:55.980
Thank you, Chieko.

00:16:59.650 --> 00:17:04.460
I hid the necklace inside 
a Christmas present.

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:14.490
It's gone... My necklace is missing!

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:19.810
The next morning, Lady Catherine 
retrieved the necklace.

00:17:21.530 --> 00:17:25.000
She claimed that she couldn't reconcile

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:28.200
with a man whose family 
treated her like a liar.

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:30.890
Lord Ashcroft accepted that,

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:33.620
leaving Young Master Richard 
with the count's family

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:36.530
and departing for the Amazon alone.

00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:40.710
In the end, I returned to Japan

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:45.460
without even saying goodbye 
to Young Master Richard.

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:49.600
At the rate I was going, I would have 
been under the count's thumb forever,

00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:51.610
unable to ever return home to Japan.

00:17:51.610 --> 00:17:56.730
So in fear, I betrayed the young master.

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.470
Transfer Call

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.470
Zoom

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.470
Hide Buttons

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.470
Menu

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.470
End

00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:04.470
Young Master Richard...

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:08.720
Richard's been looking for you this whole time.

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:12.230
Please...

00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:37.630
Chieko.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:45.050
It's been so long.

00:18:45.710 --> 00:18:47.880
And, uh...

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:51.810
What was I trying to say?

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:55.610
I can't do it... I can't find the words.

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:04.740
Chieko, I'm sorry for causing 
you pain for so long.

00:19:10.600 --> 00:19:12.760
I'm the one who should apologize.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:17.830
All I could think about 
was fleeing the manor.

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:24.100
I knew what happened wasn't your fault,

00:19:24.380 --> 00:19:29.100
and that you'd continue 
to feel responsible for it.

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:35.140
I've never been able to stop thinking 
about how cruel I was to you.

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.820
I'm so very sorry.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:42.330
"Javert, there's nothing that I blame you for."

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:45.830
"You've done your duty, nothing more."

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:50.750
Those were Jean Valjean's words to Javert.

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:54.790
Let bygones be bygones, Chieko.

00:19:56.960 --> 00:20:00.800
Thank you, Young Master Richard.

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:04.080
I'm too old to be called 
a young master anymore.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:08.120
Back then, you used to look up at me.

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:11.770
You've grown so much.

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:16.830
Chieko, I have a request.

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:19.170
Shake my hand.

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:21.440
No...

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:24.110
Allow me to embrace you.

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:46.050
Is this half of the necklace?

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:53.020
Before I returned to Japan, 
Lady Catherine left half of it behind.

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:55.450
I've never been able to return it.

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:57.760
I'm like a thief.

00:20:57.760 --> 00:20:59.020
You're wrong.

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:02.470
Just as Jean Valjean didn't steal anything,

00:21:02.470 --> 00:21:05.860
this was a gift to you from Catherine-san.

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:10.590
Was the reason he recommended 
this book to you...

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:13.800
That's right.

00:21:13.800 --> 00:21:17.080
You've made a good friend, Young Master.

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:24.840
Regarding this piece of jewelry, 
why not take this opportunity to remake it?

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:27.960
I know a skilled artisan.

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:31.220
You really have become a fine man.

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:33.680
Thanks to you.

00:21:57.210 --> 00:21:58.500
Seigi.

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:04.840
It's been a while. It's Dad.
